					<p class="mb-3">
						<span class="lang-zh">
							在经典计算中，一个晶体管里流淌着数以万计的电子，即便个别电子逃逸或受到热扰动，整体高低电平依然固若金汤。然而在量子计算中，一个量子比特（Qubit）往往就是一颗孤立的钙离子或钡离子。根据量子力学，量子信息存储在离子的能级叠加态 α|0⟩ + β|1⟩ 中。
						</span>
						<span class="lang-en">
							In classical computation, a transistor manipulates macroscopic currents composed of billions of electrons; stray thermal fluctuations barely nudge the discrete high/low voltage states. In quantum computation, however, a single qubit is often an isolated, individual ion. Quantum information lives in fragile superpositions α|0⟩ + β|1⟩.
						</span>
					</p>
					<p class="text-slate-400 text-xs sm:text-sm">
						<span class="lang-zh">
							环境中最微弱的磁场抖动、激光相位漂移、乃至极其微量的热辐射，都会在毫秒之内破坏这种精巧的相位关系（相位翻转相干时间 $T_2$ 耗尽），或是导致受激能级自发跌落（弛豫时间 $T_1$ 耗尽）。这种量子叠加态向经典随机概率的退化，被称为<strong>退相干（Decoherence）</strong>。更致命的是，量子力学中的<strong>不可克隆定理（No-Cloning Theorem）</strong>严禁复制未知量子态，这意味着经典计算中把比特复制三份取多数表决的方案在量子世界彻底失效。
						</span>
						<span class="lang-en">
							Minute environmental magnetic jitter, laser phase fluctuations, and ambient thermal radiation destroy fragile phase relationships within milliseconds ($T_2$ dephasing), or trigger spontaneous state decay ($T_1$ relaxation). This corruption is known as <strong>decoherence</strong>. Worse still, the <strong>No-Cloning Theorem</strong> strictly forbids duplicating an unknown quantum state, rendering classical triple-modular redundancy mathematically impossible in quantum states.
						</span>
					</p>
